{
  "purpose": "Qualify ordered bounded acknowledged-rate accounting and diagnose automatic format recovery",
  "passed": false,
  "repetitionsPerCase": 1,
  "productionPolicyChanged": false,
  "interpretation": [
    "Both runs use the corrected native rate window at 3742cb3, identical images and unchanged format/playback gates. The default threshold still leaves 360p after 90 seconds of recovery; it additionally retains a 194 ms baseline freeze. No host/runtime integrity gate failed, so the freeze is not dismissed as invalid measurement.",
    "Removing only the 10% encoder threshold reaches 540p, restores the 6 Mbit/s bitrate and passes all gates except final format recovery. This does not qualify a threshold-only fix.",
    "Recovery diagnostics stay in the recovery algorithm rather than additive increase. Received tracked RTP throughput is below the combined target expected by the adapter.",
    "A deterministic primary/FEC writer plus TWCC regression proves the adapter unit mismatch: 1000-byte payloads with 20-byte RTP headers each 10 ms yield 816 kbit/s acknowledged throughput, excluding the two untracked FEC packets. The adapter wrongly maps an 800 kbit/s native target to 666666 bit/s after dividing by the configured 5/1 FEC ratio.",
    "The temporary diagnostic field names at 468637b said Payload; Pion actually includes RTP headers. This curated record uses RTP names. The subsequent source correction renames the metrics and documents their exact scope.",
    "The native rate correction is independently covered by failed-before/passed-after equal-arrival, reordering and interval-boundary regressions, full race tests and lint. It is not presented as a complete recovery fix.",
    "The adapter correction and another unchanged-profile network run remain required; no new probing, larger queue or relaxed gate was introduced."
  ],
